<title>SWEDEN: Swedish Riksbank leaves rates unchanged at meeting.</title>
<headline>Swedish Riksbank leaves rates unchanged at meeting.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, said on Thursday its regular board meeting ended without any changes to its key interest rates.</p>
<p>The decision to leave the rates unchanged was in line with market expectations.</p>
<p>The central bank's lending and deposit rates currently stand at 5.25 percent and 3.75 percent, respectively, while the key repurchase rate is set at 4.10 percent.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
